    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">COPD, GOLD grade 2, group B (J44.9)</content>. Clear benefit from the LAMA with LABA and from rehabilitation: CAT 18 to 14 and mMRC 2 to 1, with less reliever use. The CT confirms centrilobular emphysema. The 4 mm nodule is benign in appearance (Lung-RADS 2). [S]<list><item>Continue umeclidinium-vilanterol and rehabilitation.</item><item>Next low-dose CT in twelve months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hyperlipidemia on atorvastatin (E78.5)</content>. LDL down from 148 to 86 mg/dL without side effects. Coronary calcification on the CT supports continuing the statin. [S]<list><item>Continue atorvastatin 20 mg; lipid panel yearly.</item><item>Report any chest pain on exertion at once.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Symptoms: CAT and mMRC dyspnea scale</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>CAT 14; mMRC 1</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Exacerbations in the past 12 months (moderate and severe) and GOLD group</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None; group B</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pulse oximetry at rest</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>95 percent on room air</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Spirometry: post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC and FEV1 % predicted (race-neutral GLI Global)</td><td>At diagnosis, then at least yearly or with a clear change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Diagnostic spirometry six weeks ago; repeat in a year</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Smoking status and cessation support</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Smoke-free</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>BMI and nutrition</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>BMI 22.7</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Inhaler technique, adherence and side effects (dry mouth, urinary retention)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Correct technique; no missed doses; no dry mouth or urinary symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Low-dose CT lung cancer screening</td><td>Yearly at 50 to 80 with 20 or more pack-years, while within fifteen years of quitting</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Done five weeks ago: Lung-RADS 2 (4 mm solid nodule); emphysema; coronary calcification; next in twelve months</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Pulmonary rehabilitation</td><td>Offer when mMRC is 2 or more, or CAT 10 or more; within three weeks of a hospital discharge for an exacerbation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Eight of twenty sessions completed</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel after starting a statin</td><td>Four to twelve weeks after starting, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 158, HDL 46, LDL 86, triglycerides 130 mg/dL</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Statin safety: muscle symptoms</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No muscle aches</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>ECG and cardiovascular risk</td><td>At baseline; reassess after exacerbations</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal ECG at intake; coronary calcification noted on CT; no angina</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccines: influenza, pneumococcal, RSV, COVID-19, Tdap, zoster</td><td>Yearly review</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza, RSV, COVID-19 and zoster at the wellness visit in four weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Long-term oxygen assessment</td><td>When resting PaO2 is 55 mm Hg or less (60 with cor pulmonale or polycythemia) or saturation 88 percent or less, confirmed twice</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Saturation 95 percent; no change since the blood gas</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find the cause of the breathlessness. Outcome by 2026-07-28: COPD confirmed by spirometry (post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC 0.58); heart failure unlikely (NT-proBNP 92, normal ECG); alpha-1 antitrypsin normal [S]</item><item>Walk farther with less breathlessness. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>Fewer and milder flare-ups, treated early. In progress; target 2027-07-14 [S]</item><item>LDL below 100 mg/dL. Outcome by 2026-09-08: LDL 148 to 86 mg/dL on atorvastatin 20 mg [S]</item><item>Vaccines up to date. In progress; target 2026-10-06 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for the Prevention, Diagnosis and Management of COPD: 2025 Report (2025); Race and Ethnicity in Pulmonary Function Test Interpretation: An Official American Thoracic Society Statement (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, COPD and hyperlipidemia monographs (2026); Pulmonary Rehabilitation for Adults with Chronic Respiratory Disease: An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2023); Home Oxygen Therapy for Adults with Chronic Lung Disease: An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2020); A Randomized Trial of Long-Term Oxygen for COPD with Moderate Desaturation (LOTT) (2016); Racial Bias in Pulse Oximetry Measurement (2020); Lung Cancer: Screening (2021); Statin Use for the Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease in Adults: Preventive Medication (2022); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Wellness visit with vaccines in four weeks. Fifteen-week review in seven weeks. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

